From e8404bf57ff7b40fb95a09275dedf9b913306747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark <30506876+markhuguet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:31:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] inkling: MTP depth heads + short-conv state rollback

- load the 8 MTP depth layers (blk.n_layer.., nextn.eh_proj/enorm/hnorm, dense FFN)
  and build the MTP graph: eh_proj(cat[hnorm(h) | enorm(tok_norm(embd(x)))]) -> decoder layer,
  shared LM head, no final norm; target exports post-final-norm hidden as h_nextn
- recurrent memory sized over n_layer_all; hybrid memories filter MTP / backbone layers by ctx type
- short-conv rollback snapshots (n_rs_seq) in build_sconv; Inkling joins llm_arch_supports_rs_rollback
- llama_memory_seq_rewind_nextn: position-only rewind used by the MTP chain-heads catch-up and draft
- MTP draft context gets the target's n_rs_seq so common_memory::seq_rm can roll both back
- tools/inkling-mtp-check: teacher-forced per-depth MTP accuracy check

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
